{
    "background_story": "Santos was a skilled Spanish pilot who flew with the Luftwaffe during World War II. Born in Madrid, he was fascinated by aircraft and mechanics from a young age. After the Spanish Civil War, Santos joined the German air force, drawn by their advanced technology and tactics. He quickly proved himself to be an exceptional pilot, earning the respect of his comrades and the admiration of his superiors. Santos flew numerous missions over the Eastern Front, demonstrating bravery and skill in the face of overwhelming odds. Despite the chaos and destruction around him, he remained committed to his duty and his fellow airmen. After the war, Santos returned to Spain, where he kept a low profile, haunted by the memories of the conflict. His experiences as a Luftwaffe pilot left an indelible mark on his life, a reminder of the complexities of war and loyalty.",
